TTYCHATTER C COMMAND-LINE CLIENT
================================

This directory contains the traditional Unix command-line C implementation of
ttychatter.  It is intentionally different from the Python ncurses interface:
there is no full-screen UI here.  The user supplies an input file and an output
session file.

    ttychatter input.txt output.log

The output file is also the session state.  Reusing the same output file resumes
the conversation by sending recent turns as context.

Build requirements
------------------

Debian/Ubuntu/ChromeOS Linux:

    sudo apt-get install build-essential pkg-config libcurl4-openssl-dev libjson-c-dev ca-certificates gnupg

Build:

    make

Run:

    ./ttychatter --help

First steps
-----------

    ./ttychatter --set-api-key --gpg
    ./ttychatter --doctor
    ./ttychatter --update-models
    ./ttychatter --models --search free
    ./ttychatter --test-model openrouter/auto

Then create an input file and session:

    cat > input.txt
    Explain Unix pipes in one paragraph.
    ^D

    ./ttychatter input.txt session.log

Read WALKTHROUGH for a complete step-by-step guide.
